## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, globally distributed telemetry store with practical sharding, replication, and failover strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Two-level sharding (region then device_id)
- Multi-region replication with bounded staleness
- Online shard rebalancing without downtime
- Read-after-write guarantees in local region
- Regional failover and cross-region replay trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// shard key resolver
function shardKey(region, deviceId, shardsPerRegion){
  const key = region + '|' + deviceId;
  let h = 0; for (let i = 0; i < key.length; i++) { h = (h * 31 + key.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0; }
  return h % shardsPerRegion;
}
```

```javascript
async function writeEvent(event){
  const shard = shardKey(event.region, event.deviceId, regionConfig[event.region].shards);
  await writeToShard(event, shard, {consistency: 'quorum'});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would clock skew across regions affect bounds on staleness?
- What metrics would you use to verify online rebalancing safety and latency budgets?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of a beginner-friendly, real-world saga with event-sourcing and CQRS: how to coordinate cross-service work, model event contracts, and ensure idempotent handlers with an outbox.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration vs choreography in a write-side workflow
- Event contracts and read-model sketching for status tracking
- Outbox pattern and correlation-based deduplication

## Code Example
```javascript
// Map write events to commands (simplified)
function mapEventToCommand(evt){
  switch(evt.type){
    case 'ContentSubmitted':
      return { type: 'ModerationRequest', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId, correlationId: evt.id } }
    case 'ModerationApproved':
      return { type: 'PublishContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
    case 'ModerationRejected':
      return { type: 'HideContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
  }
}

// Deduplication (idempotent handler)
if (outbox.has(correlationId)) return; outbox.add(correlationId);
```

